Your organization's ID ( ) and API key ( ) can be reused in future API calls after they have been initially generated. However, your access token ( ) is temporary and must be regenerated every 24 hours.

When using list (GET) endpoints in the Reactor API, you may find it necessary to limit the returned results to a subset of records. To accomplish this, many of the API's list endpoints support the ability to filter by specific attributes.

To filter the response for a given list endpoint, you must supply a query parameter in the request path.

GET {ENDPOINT}?filter[{ATTRIBUTE_NAME}]={OPERATOR} {VALUE}

Property
Description
{ENDPOINT}
A listing endpoint in the Reactor API that supports filter parameters.
{ATTRIBUTE_NAME}
The name of a specific attribute to filter results by. Keep in mind that different endpoints support different attributes for filtering.

Note that if the structure of your filters is incorrect, no filters are applied and the full result set is returned.

