You can create media sessions in Web SDK in two ways:
- allow the Web SDK to manage the dispatch of media ping events to . The frequency of these pings is determined by the configuration settings of the component.  
Automatically-tracked media sessions  
Adobe Analytics for Streaming Media  

To start tracking a media session automatically, call the method with the options described below:  
createMediaSession  
alloy("createMediaSession", {
        playerId: "movie-test",
        getPlayerDetails: () => {
            return {
                playhead: document.getElementById("movie-test").currentTime,
                qoeDataDetails: {
                    bitrate: 1000,
                    startupTime: 1000,
                    fps: 30,
                    droppedFrames: 10
                }
            };
        },
        xdm: {
            eventType: "media.sessionStart",
            mediaCollection: {
                sessionDetails: {
                    ...
                }
            }
        }
    });  

Property  
Type  
Required  
Description  
playerId  
String  
Yes  
The player ID, an unique identifier representing the media session.  
getPlayerDetails  
Function  
Yes  
A function that returns the player details. This callback function will be called by the Web SDK before every media event for the provided.  
playerId  
xdm.eventType  
Object  
No  
The media event type. If not provided, this field is automatically set to .  
media.sessionStart  
xdm.mediaCollection.sessionDetails  
Object  
Yes  
