The Experience Cloud Identity (ECID) is a persistent identifier assigned to a user when they visit your website. In certain circumstances, you might prefer to access the ECID (to send it to a third party, for example). Another use case is setting the ECID in a custom XDM field, in addition to having it in the identity map.

You can access the ECID either via (recommended) or via tags.

If you need to access the ECID on the client side, use the tags approach as described below:

Ensure your property is configured with enabled.
Create a new rule. This rule should be used exclusively for capturing the ECID without any other important actions.
Add a Library Loaded event to the rule.
Add a Custom Code action to the rule with the following code (assuming the name you've configured for the SDK instance is and there isn't already a data element of the same name):

code language-js
return alloy("getIdentity")
   .then(function(result) {
     _satellite.setVar("ECID", result.identity.ECID);
   });

Save the rule.

You should then be able to access the ECID in subsequent rules using or , like you would access any other data element.

