On before event send callback

A callback function to evaluate and modify the payload sent to Adobe. Within the code editor, you have access to the following variables:

: The XDM payload for the event.
content.xdm
: The data object payload for the event.
content.data
: Immediately exit the callback and send data to Adobe with the current values in the object.
return true content
: Immediately exit the callback and abort sending data to Adobe.
return false

Any variables defined outside of can be used, but are not included in the payload sent to Adobe.
content

WARNING
This callback allows the use of custom code. If any code that you include in the callback throws an uncaught exception, processing for the event halts.
Data is not sent to Adobe.

// Use nullish coalescing assignments to add objects if they don't yet exist
content.xdm.commerce ??= {};
content.xdm.commerce.order ??= {};

// Then add the purchase ID
content.xdm.commerce.order.purchaseID = "12345";

// Use optional chaining to prevent undefined errors when setting tracking code to lower case
if(content.xdm.marketing?.trackingCode) content.xdm.marketing.trackingCode = content.xdm.marketing.trackingCode.toLowerCase();

// Delete operating system version
if(content.xdm.environment) delete content.xdm.environment.operatingSystemVersion;

// Immediately end onBeforeEventSend logic and send the data to Adobe for this event type
if (content.xdm.eventType === "web.webInteraction.linkClicks") {
  return true;
}

// Cancel sending data if it is a known bot
if (myBotDetector.isABot()) {
  return false;
}

TIP
Avoid returning on the first event on a page. Returning on the first event can negatively impact personalization.

