Views in web extensionsEach event, condition, action, or data element type may provide a view allowing a user to supply settings. The extension may also have a top-level which allows users to supply global settings for the entire extension. The process of building a view is identical across all types of views.

Registering with the extension bridge communication APIAfter the iframe script is loaded, you will need to provide some methods to tags which it will use for communication. Call and pass it an object as follows:

window.extensionBridge.register({
  init: function(info) {
    // Populate view with info.settings which will exist if the user is editing something
    // that was previously saved.
    if (info.settings) {
      document.getElementById('name').value = info.settings.name;
    }
  },
