Purchase parameters are passed on an order confirmation page after a successful order and are used for Target conversion and optimization goals. With a Platform Web SDK implementation, these parameters and are automatically mapped from XDM data passed as part of the field group.

at.js example using targetPageParams():
targetPageParams = function() {
  return {
    "orderId": "ABC123",
    "productPurchasedId": "SKU-00002,SKU-00003"
    "orderTotal": 1337.89
  };
};

Purchase information is passed to Target when the field group has set to. The order ID and order total are automatically mapped from the object. If the array is present, then the values are use for.

Platform Web SDK example using sendEvent:
alloy("sendEvent", {
  "xdm": {
    "commerce": {
      "order": {
        "purchaseID": "ABC123",
        "priceTotal": 1337.89
      },
      "purchases": {
        "value": 1
      }
    },
    "productListItems": [{
      "SKU": "SKU-00002"
    }, {
      "SKU": "SKU-00003"
    }],
      "_experience": {
          "decisioning": {
              "propositions": [{
                  "scope": "<your_mbox>"
              }],
              "propositionEventType": {
