Retrieving failed batches using the Data Access API

Adobe Experience Platform provides two methods for uploading and ingesting data. You can either use batch ingestion, which allows you to insert their data using various file types (such as CSVs), or streaming ingestion, which allows you to insert their data to Experience Platform using streaming endpoints in real time.  

Retrieve the failed batch
API format  
GET /batches/{BATCH_ID}/failed  

Request  
curl -X GET 'https://platform.adobe.io/data/foundation/export/batches/{BATCH_ID}/failed' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer {ACCESS_TOKEN}' \
  -H 'Cache-Control: no-cache' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -H 'x-api-key: {API_KEY}' \
  -H 'x-gw-ims-org-id: {ORG_ID}' \
  -H 'x-sandbox-name: {SANDBOX_NAME}'  

Response  
{
    "data": [
        {
            "name": "part-00000-44c7b669-5e38-43fb-b56c-a0686dabb982-c000.json",
            "length": "1800",
            "_links": {
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://platform.adobe.io:443/data/foundation/export/batches/{BATCH_ID}/failed?path=part-00000-44c7b669-5e38-43fb-b56c-a0686dabb982-c000.json"
                }
            }
